uarantees, establish any upstream authentication and access controls; the inspected runtime only supplies caller-provided X-Actor and internal-network deployment. Discovery leads, not verified facts: the support leads and service owners, team workspace or channels, internal reporting and notification documentation, and any relevant private repositories; no specific channel, site or owner was identified. Interaction and state: agents act through HTTP, requesters receive relay messages, operators view audit and outbox; shared service state lasts until process exit without DATA_FILE and across restarts with it, while sent and dead outbox records remain; requester isolation is required for batches, and no stronger access control is assumed. Intake is read-only and starts no server; the outcome will be usable in the target service checkout on final return and in a deployed target only after release."
